% THE YOLOv13 DISTRIBUTION QUESTION. Added 2026-08-15.
%
% This closes a search item that was open since 2026-08-14. The claim -- that
% YOLOv13 is not provided by the Ultralytics package and lives in a separate
% distribution -- was REMOVED from 5.1 and 7.1 as unsourced, then reintroduced
% in weaker words by a later rewrite, and is now grounded. Three sources, all
% checked on 2026-08-15:
%
%   1. The repository below. Its README states: "The code is based on
%      [Ultralytics](https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics). Thanks for
%      their excellent work!" It is a separate repository under a different
%      owner, not a module inside the package. Licence AGPL-3.0.
%   2. Ultralytics issues 21181 ("Yolov 13 has been released") and 21243
%      ("Integrating YOLOv13 Models Into Ultralytics Python Package!"), both
%      requesting integration, BOTH CLOSED AS NOT PLANNED. Neither page shows a
%      maintainer statement explaining the decision, so they evidence that
%      integration was declined, not why.
%   3. yolov13 above, the architecture paper, already cited.
%
% NO CITATION.cff AND NO ZENODO DOI exist for the repository, so it is cited as
% software with a URL and an access date. Checked directly, not assumed.
